If you want to understand the U.S. Navy like a naval strategist or senior naval commander, you need to learn its terminology across warfare communities, ship operations, fleet organization, naval aviation, intelligence, communications, logistics, and maritime strategy.

The Navy has its own language. Sailors use terms that often have entirely different meanings from their Army equivalents.

